{"name":"Tonka Bean","hex":"#6b524c","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"tonka bean","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A black wrinkled seed of a neotropical legume tree of species Dipteryx odorata, used as a perfume and vanilla substitute due to its high coumarin content."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tonka_bean"}],"entries":[{"title":"Dipteryx odorata","blocks":[{"text":"Dipteryx odorata is a species of flowering tree in the pea family, Fabaceae. The tree is native to Northern South America and is semi-deciduous. Its seeds are known as tonka beans, but sometimes spelled tonkin beans or tonquin beans. The seeds are black and wrinkled and have a smooth, brown interior. They have a strong fragrance similar to sweet woodruff due to their high content of coumarin."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/82/Flowering_Tonka_Bean_tree_%28Dipteryx_odorata%29.jpg/330px-Flowering_Tonka_Bean_tree_%28Dipteryx_odorata%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dipteryx_odorata","wikidata":"Q901484"},{"title":"Tonka","blocks":[{"text":"Tonka is an American brand and former manufacturer of toy trucks. The company was founded in 1946 and operated as an independent manufacturer of popular steel toy construction-type trucks and machinery, until its sale to Hasbro in 1991."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tonka","wikidata":"Q1645436"},{"title":"Bean","blocks":[{"text":"A bean is the seed of plants in many genera of the legume family (Fabaceae) used as a vegetable for human consumption or animal feed. The seeds are sold fresh or preserved through drying (a pulse). Beans have been cultivated since the seventh millennium BCE in Thailand, and since the second millennium BCE in Europe and in Peru. Most beans, with the exception of peas, are summer crops. As legumes, the plants fix nitrogen and form seeds with a high protein content. They are produced on a scale of millions of tons annually in many countries, with India as the largest producer."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/French_beans_J1.JPG/330px-French_beans_J1.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bean","wikidata":"Q379813"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Cumaru_%28Dipteryx_odorata%29%2C_Vaca_Diez%2C_Bolivia_1.jpg/500px-Cumaru_%28Dipteryx_odorata%29%2C_Vaca_Diez%2C_Bolivia_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Cumaru_%28Dipteryx_odorata%29%2C_Vaca_Diez%2C_Bolivia_1.jpg/1280px-Cumaru_%28Dipteryx_odorata%29%2C_Vaca_Diez%2C_Bolivia_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Cumaru_%28Dipteryx_odorata%29%2C_Vaca_Diez%2C_Bolivia_1.jpg/500px-Cumaru_%28Dipteryx_odorata%29%2C_Vaca_Diez%2C_Bolivia_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Dipteryx odorata","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACumaru_(Dipteryx_odorata)%2C_Vaca_Diez%2C_Bolivia_1.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/56/The_smooth_brown_inside_of_the_tonka_bean.jpg/500px-The_smooth_brown_inside_of_the_tonka_bean.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/56/The_smooth_brown_inside_of_the_tonka_bean.jpg/500px-The_smooth_brown_inside_of_the_tonka_bean.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The smooth brown inside of the tonka bean","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AThe_smooth_brown_inside_of_the_tonka_bean.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/1960%27s_Tonka_Truck.JPG/500p